[{"id":3789603060,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7h4MD0","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?u=af70f5d107e9c1447f296643d5a566dab53d25e8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","login":"AThousandShips","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116199#pullrequestreview-3789603060","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116199","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-02-12T09:01:42Z"},{"id":3805051981,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7izHxN","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","login":"Ivorforce","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce"},"body":"Looks good overall, though it's quite a lot so I skimmed some parts. Hopefully others can help with review too.\n\nA general observation: It's good to be precise and use the correct terminology, but remember that Godot is primarily for game devs. More than in dedicated audio software, it can be good to explain things with simple or redundant words (like \"volume level\" instead of \"level\") as developers may not be aware of the 'correct' lingo.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116199#pullrequestreview-3805051981","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116199","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-02-15T15:30:54Z"},{"id":3805260561,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7iz6sR","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?u=64fc5e539030609be0447a74243d9fc643fa9bf3&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","login":"Meorge","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge"},"body":"Looks good! Sounds like there is a lot of helpful technical info in here.\n\nI recognize this could be considered out of scope for this PR (it's quite big and impressive already!) but, *if feasible*, I think it could be nice to add some more basic descriptions to the audio effects; for example, use cases of each one that a developer not familiar with audio might want to implement for their game. (Once again though, I recognize this could be a big ask for an already-big PR, so perhaps it'd be best to do in a follow-up 😅)","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116199#pullrequestreview-3805260561","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116199","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-02-15T18:31:10Z"},{"id":3805300319,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7i0EZf","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","login":"Ivorforce","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"